  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: HTTP/2 flow control window overflow leading to\n     heap buffer overflow\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-123007.patch: account for queued frames\n       when validating WINDOW_UPDATE\n     - CVE-2026-123007\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free in the resolver when the same name\n     is resolved in subrequests\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-123634.patch: fix non-current resolve\n       finalization from resolve handler\n     - CVE-2026-123634\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free in the mail proxy\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-113425.patch: block client writes while\n       waiting for auth_http, upstream and SMTP client resolving\n     - CVE-2026-113425\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: buffer overflow with try_files and alias\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-125283.patch: recalculate the length after\n       running the script\n     - CVE-2026-125283\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: endless loop while reading the request body over\n     SSL\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-118899.patch: explicit handling of\n       NGX_AGAIN\n     - CVE-2026-118899\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: ClientHello parsing differential in ssl_preread\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-123640.patch: forbid trailing data in\n       extensions and duplicate SNI/ALPN\n     - CVE-2026-123640",
